        "Furthermore, the event serves as a chronological marker in Islamic history. Since the Arabs did not use a fixed calendar at the time, they dated events relative to this year. Most importantly, the preservation of the Ka'bah ensured that the Qibla of the future Ummah would remain intact, free from the hegemony of the Byzantine or Sassanid-backed proxies. The story continues to be recited by millions of Muslims daily in their prayers, signifying that no earthly power can overcome the Will of Allah.",
