        "Her life intersected with that of Prophet Sulayman (AS), the son of Dawud (AS), who governed a vast empire from Yerushalayim (Jerusalem). Sulayman (AS) was granted unique miracles, including command over the jinn, animals, and the wind. The encounter between these two powerful monarchs remains one of the most profound narratives in the Qur'an, symbolizing the triumph of divine truth over material grandeur and the submission of human sovereignty to the Absolute Sovereignty of Allah.",
