        "The event at the festival grounds became the catalyst for the eventual destabilization of Pharaoh’s ideological grip on Egypt. Their martyrdom served as a silent invitation to the secret believers within the palace, including Pharaoh’s wife, Asiya, and the Believer from the family of Pharaoh. They left behind a template for the 'Tawba' (repentance) that is accepted even at the last moment of one's previous life.",
